we start in india where at least 18  people were killed and more than a  hundred injured when a passenger plane  skidded off the runway  in the southern city of corricode the  air india express flight from dubai was  carrying  190 passengers and crew heavy monsoon  rain appears to have had a role in the  crash  eyewitnesses described the plane's  fuselage breaking apart as it fell into  a valley some 10 meters below  the boeing 737 flight from dubai was  repatriating  indian citizens stranded by the  coronavirus pandemic  a disastrous outcome for passengers that  had waited months to fly home and  reunite with their families  among the victims were the two pilots as  well as at least one young child  i found a child under a box on the plane  as soon as i picked her up her head had  serious injuries  small child one and a half years old i  took the child in the car  if she was in the ambulance maybe she  could have been saved  i took her to the hospital but she died  [Music]  the remaining passengers and crew  rescued from the rubble are being  treated at several hospitals in the city  many are in critical condition  [Music]  indian prime minister modi tweeted his  condolences to the families of the  victims  heavy rain has battered the area in  recent days and may have caused the  aircraft to overshoot the runway  officials say that whilst rescue  operations are  over they fear the death toll could rise  well joining us now from the indian  capital delhi is dw correspondent amisha  jaiswal  namisha do we know anything more about  the condition of those injured in the  crash  well anthony at least 18 deaths have  already been reported  after rescue operations took over three  hours and all the passengers were  evacuated  dozens of passengers have also been  injured and at least 15 of these  are seriously injured according to  reports from the police  on the ground now these fish these  injured  victims have been taken to hospitals in  corigote itself as well as the  